Timeline
- Found while assessing what enforcement survives without GitHub rulesets:
  tracing which workflow actually evaluates each guard.
- Verified independently before acting: grep showed check-runs present only
  in promote.yml, and promote.yml's 'if:' is the staging:passed label.
- The interesting part is the direction of the drift. spec.org and the TLA+
  model both said guard 2 has no bypass, and the model enforced it on both
  transitions. Only the YAML disagreed. Design-level verification does not
  transfer to the implementation for free.

Reproduction
  grep -n 'check-runs' .github/workflows/*.yml
    -> promote.yml only (before)
    -> promote.yml + deploy-production.yml (after)
  grep -n 'if:' .github/workflows/promote.yml
    -> if: github.event.label.name == 'staging:passed'
